Description: native YouTube Music desktop client
 Melyar is a lightweight YouTube Music client for Linux. A Rust core handles
 the InnerTube API, the stream cipher, mpv playback, the local library and the
 Linux desktop integration, a Qt 6 shell hosts it, and a React interface draws
 it.
 .
 It speaks to YouTube Music directly, so it needs no account of its own and no
 cloud service. Playback runs through libmpv, the library is kept in a local
 SQLite database, and the interface speaks twelve languages.
 .
 The client integrates with the desktop rather than sitting on top of it:
 MPRIS for media keys, a Unix socket for Waybar and Polybar, global shortcuts
 and a desktop entry.
